title: 'statement-store: keep the recovery replay when the filter changes during major sync'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a node in major sync drops every incoming statement, and afterwards it
    repeats its affinity filter so that each peer sends everything again. If an RPC client
    subscribed or unsubscribed during the sync, the filter differed, each peer sent only the
    difference, and the statements dropped on the unchanged topics stayed missing. Now the node
    sends the filter that it advertised last ahead of the changed one, and a peer that sees a
    repeated filter sends everything for the filter that follows it. A newly connected peer
    receives the filter of the last broadcast.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
